      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\((-1)^k = -1\\) for odd \\(k\\) and \\((-1)^k = 1\\) for even \\(k,\\) the terms alternate \\(-1, 1, -1, 1, \\ldots\\)\n\nThere are \\(2006\\) terms, forming \\(1003\\) pairs, each equal to \\((-1) + 1 = 0.\\) The total is \\(0.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
